"Second Semi-Final result | EBU (https://www.ebu.ch/news/2011/second-semi-final-result)\nciteturn35view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ebu.ch/news/2011/second-semi-final-result\",\"lineno\":75}); Total lines: 220\nL42: (Note: Translations are generated with the help of AI without human review. These translations are made available to you for convenience and may contain inaccuracies or errors. Please check important information in the original English version or contact us. The EBU cannot be held liable for any inaccuracies or errors contained in these translations.)\nL43: \nL44: Languages 【57†English】【58†Français】\nL45: \nL46: Member login required Powered by Eurovox\nL47: 【59†عربي】【59†български】【59†Čeština】【59†Deutsch】【59†Español】【59†עברית】【59†Hrvatski】【59†Italiano】【59†ελληνικά】【59†Magyar】【59†Nederlands】【59†Polski】【59†Portuguęs】【59†Română】【59†Pусский】【59†Shqip】【59†Suomi】【59†Svenska】【59†Türkçe】【59†Yкраїнська】\nL48: \nL49: Translation in progress\nL50: \nL51: 【59†Not signed in】\nL52: \nL53: Dear user,\nL54: \nL55: EBU switched to a new authentication method, Microsoft Entra.\nL56: For most EBU Members: You can now log in with your work email and password (federated login) instead of a separate EBU account. On the login screen, enter your professional email; you'll be redirected to your organization's login page.\nL57: \nL58: Shared mailboxes: No longer supported. If you use one, you'll need to create an individual account (see instructions below).\nL59: \nL60: If federated login doesn't work: You'll be redirected based on your email:\nL61:   * Linked to Microsoft → log in via login.live.com\nL62:   * Linked to Google → log in via accounts.google.com\nL63:   * Neither → a temporary password will be emailed to you each time\nL64: \nL65: Creating a new account: Select \"No account? Create one\" and choose Microsoft (recommended for EBU Member staff), Google, or another email address. Note: this choice can't be changed later.\nL66: \nL67: Still stuck? Contact 【60†[email protected]】.\nL68: \nL69: \nL70: \nL71: \nL72: \nL73: \nL74: \nL75: 【61†Back to Stories】 STORIES\nL76: # Second Semi-Final result\nL77: \nL78: 13 May 2011\nL79: \nL80: 【62†Image: Second Semi-Final result 】\nL81: \nL82: Second Semi-Final result: All 25 Eurovision Song Contents Finalists chosen\nL83: \nL84: Düsseldorf, Thursday 12 May 2011 – The second batch of 10 countries qualified for the Final of the 56th Eurovision Song Contest tonight. The second Semi-Final was broadcast live over the Eurovision network in the 19 countries taking part this evening plus Germany, France and Italy.\nL85: The following 25 countries will compete in Saturday’s Final, given in the running order (second Semi-Final qualifiers in bold):\nL86: \nL87: 1. Finland\nL88: 2. Bosnia & Herzegovina\nL89: 3. Denmark\nL90: 4. Lithuania\nL91: 5. Hungary\nL92: 6. Ireland\nL93: 7. Sweden\nL94: 8. Estonia\nL95: 9. Greece\nL96: 10. Russia\nL97: 11. France\nL98: 12. Italy\nL99: 13. Switzerland\nL100: 14. United Kingdom\nL101: 15. Moldova\nL102: 16. Germany\nL103: 17. Romania\nL104: 18. Austria\nL105: 19. Azerbaijan\nL106: 20. Slovenia\nL107: 21. Iceland\nL108: 22. Spain\nL109: 23. Ukraine\nL110: 24. Serbia\nL111: 25. Georgia\nL112: All the qualifiers were determined in a mixed vote by televoters and juries (comprising 5 music industry professionals) in all of tonight’s 19 participating countries as well as viewers and juries in Italy, France, and Germany.\nL113: On Tuesday 10 May, the first batch of 10 countries qualified (in order of announcement): Serbia, Lithuania, Greece, Azerbaijan, Georgia, Switzerland, Hungary, Finland, Russia and Iceland. Under the rules, five countries automatically qualify for Saturday's Final: Italy, Spain, United Kingdom and France, plus the host country Germany.\nL114: Saturday’s winner will be chosen in a mixed vote by juries and televoters in all 43 countries to have taken part in the three events. It will be broadcast by all 43 participating broadcasters, as well as in several other countries around the world. Last year more than 110 million people tuned in to watch Europe’s favourite TV show, held in Oslo.\nL115: \nL116: For more details please refer to 【63†www.eurovision.tv.†www.eurovision.tv】\nL117: \nL118: -------\nL119: Note to editors:\nL120: The Eurovision Song Contest is an annual competition for active Members of the European Broadcasting Union (EBU), represented by the public broadcasters in their respective countries. The first contest was held in Lugano Switzerland in 1956. Since then, the contest has become a true European tradition. In 2011, the 56th contest will be held in Düsseldorf, Germany. News and information about the Eurovision Song Contest is available on: 【63†www.eurovision.tv†www.eurovision.tv】 .\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSecond Semi-Final result All 25 finalists of 55th Eurovision Song Contest chosen | EBU (https://www.ebu.ch/fr/news/2010/second-semi-final-result--all-25)\nciteturn35view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ebu.ch/fr/news/2010/second-semi-final-result--all-25\",\"lineno\":75}); Total lines: 213\nL56: Pour la majorité des Membres de l'UER : vous pouvez désormais vous connecter avec votre adresse e-mail et votre mot de passe professionnels (connexion fédérée) au lieu d'un compte UER distinct. Sur l'écran de connexion, saisissez votre adresse e-mail professionnelle ; vous serez redirigé vers la page de connexion de votre organisation.\nL57: \nL58: Boîtes mail partagées : elles ne sont plus prises en charge. Si vous en utilisez une, vous devrez créer un compte individuel (voir les instructions ci-dessous).\nL59: Si la connexion fédérée ne fonctionne pas : vous serez redirigé selon votre adresse e-mail :\nL60: \nL61:   * Liée à Microsoft → connexion via login.live.com\nL62:   * Liée à Google → connexion via accounts.google.com\nL63:   * Ni l'une ni l'autre → un mot de passe temporaire vous sera envoyé par e-mail à chaque connexion\nL64: Création d'un nouveau compte : sélectionnez « Pas de compte ? Créez-en un » et choisissez Microsoft (recommandé pour le personnel des Membres), Google, ou une autre adresse e-mail. Attention : ce choix ne pourra pas être modifié ultérieurement.\nL65: \nL66: Besoin d'aide ? Contactez 【60†[email protected]】.\nL67: \nL68: \nL69: \nL70: \nL71: \nL72: \nL73: \nL74: 【61†Retour à Histoires】 HISTOIRES\nL75: # Second Semi-Final result All 25 finalists of 55th Eurovision Song Contest chosen\nL76: \nL77: 28 mai 2010\nL78: \nL79: Oslo, Thursday 27 May 2010 – The second Semi-Final of the 2010 Eurovision Song Contest took place in Oslo tonight, and was broadcast live on television via the Eurovision network in all tonight’s participating countries, United Kingdom and Norway. Contestants from 10 countries qualified for the Final of Europe's favourite TV-show.\nL80: Representatives from the following 25 countries qualified for the Final, given in the running order (qualifiers from the second Semi-Final in bold):\nL81: 1. Azerbaijan\nL82: 2. Spain\nL83: 3. Norway\nL84: 4. Moldova\nL85: 5. Cyprus【62†Image】\nL86: 6. Bosnia & Herzegovina\nL87: 7. Belgium\nL88: 8. Serbia\nL89: 9. Belarus\nL90: 10. Ireland\nL91: 11. Greece\nL92: 12. The United Kingdom\nL93: 13. Georgia\nL94: 14. Turkey\nL95: 15. Albania\nL96: 16. Iceland\nL97: 17. Ukraine\nL98: 18. France\nL99: 19. Romania\nL100: 20. Russia\nL101: 21. Armenia\nL102: 22. Germany\nL103: 23. Portugal\nL104: 24. Israel\nL105: 25. Denmark\nL106: All the qualifiers were determined by a mixed vote by televoters and juries (5 music industry professionals) in all tonight’s 17 participating countries as well as viewers and juries in Norway and the United Kingdom.\nL107: This Tuesday, 25 May, 10 countries qualified for the Final: Bosnia & Herzegovina, Moldova, Russia, Greece, Portugal, Belarus, Serbia, Belgium, Albania and Iceland. Five countries were already in the line up for Saturday's Final. Germany, Spain, United Kingdom and France, plus the host country Norway, qualify automatically under the rules.\nL108: A total of 25 countries will take part in the Final, which will be held in Oslo this Saturday, 29 May 2010 (21:00 CET). The winner will be chosen by a mixed voting between juries and televoters in all the participating countries. The Final will be broadcast by all the 39 participating broadcasters, as well as in Hungary, Kazakhstan, Burma, Australia, Montenegro, New Zealand and Kosovo. Last year 125 million people tuned in to watch Europe’s favourite TV-show, held in Moscow, Russia.\nL109: For more details please refer to 【63†www.eurovision.tv†www.eurovision.tv】.\nL110: Note to editors:\nL111: \nL112: Eurovision TV is a brand of the European Broadcasting Union (EBU)\nL113: The European Broadcasting Union (EBU) serves 86 national media organizations from 56 countries in and around Europe. It promotes the values and distinctiveness of public service media in Europe and around the world. It brings news, sports, events and music to your home through the Eurovision and Euroradio networks. The EBU develops and shares best practices, media expertise and innovation. It produces and exchanges rich and diverse programmes across all media. 【64†www.ebu.ch】\nL114: # Liens et documents pertinents\nL115: \nL116: ## Related news\nL117: \nL118: ## Communiqués\nL119: \nL120: 【65†Concours Eurovision de la Chanson 2025 : la composition des demi-finales confirmée】\nL121: \nL122: La composition des demi-finales du Concours Eurovision de la Chanson (CEC) de cette année a été déterminée par tirage au sort lors de la cérémonie officielle...\nL123: \nL124: 28 janvier 2025\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEurovision 2017: Running order in the Grand Final decided (https://eurovisionworld.com/esc/eurovision-2017-running-order-in-grand-final-decided)\nciteturn35view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://eurovisionworld.com/esc/eurovision-2017-running-order-in-grand-final-decided\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 60\nL0:  | 【0†Eurovision News】【1†Junior Eurovision】【2†Eurovision Asia】【3†Burgas 2027】【4†Calendar】【5†National Selections】【6†Tickets】【7†Results & Points】【8†Odds】【9†Songs & Videos】【10†Polls】【11†Stats】【12†Winners】【13†Facts】【14†Quiz】【15†OGAE】select year/country  |\nL1: \nL2: \nL3: \nL4: 【16†Image: Eurovision 2017 Running Order Planning†pix.eurovisionworld.com】\nL5: \nL6: 【17†RUNNING ORDER】\nL7: \nL8: # Eurovision 2017: Running order in the Grand Final decided\nL9: ## From Israel to France. The running order in Saturday's Grand Final of Eurovision Song Contest 2017 has been decided. Like the four previous years, the producer of Eurovision Song Contest decides the running order\nL10: \nL11: 12 May 2017\nL12: \nL13: Tags:【17†Running order】【18†Kyiv 2017】【19†Draw】【20†Grand Final】【21†UA:PBC】【22†EBU】\nL14: The producer of this years Eurovision, the Ukrainian broadcaster UA:PBC, has decided the running order for the Grand Final at Eurovision Song Contest 2017. The last four years the producers of the shows have decided the running order based on an allocation draw. The 【23†allocation draw took place】 shortly after 【24†Semi-final 1】 and 【25†Semi-final 2】. Here the participants were distributed in the first or second half of the Grand Final.\nL15: ### Running order\nL16: \nL17: 【26†EUROVISION 2017 • RUNNING ORDERGrand Final • 13 May 2017】\nL18: \nL19: 【27†1Israel】【28†2Poland】【29†3Belarus】【30†4Austria】【31†5Armenia】【32†6Netherlands】【33†7Moldova】【34†8Hungary】【35†9Italy】【36†10Denmark】【37†11Portugal】【38†12Azerbaijan】【39†13Croatia】\nL20: \nL21: 【40†14Australia】【41†15Greece】【42†16Spain】【43†17Norway】【44†18United Kingdom】【45†19Cyprus】【46†20Romania】【47†21Germany】【48†22Ukraine】【49†23Belgium】【50†24Sweden】【51†25Bulgaria】【52†26France】\nL22: ### How is the running order decided?\nL23: \nL24: Right after the 10 qualifiers from the second Semi-final are known, the producer of the contest starts laying the puzzle to ensure variety in the Grand Final.\nL25: ### Eurovision Song Contest 2017\nL26: \nL27: The 62nd Eurovision Song Contest takes place on 9, 11 and 13 May 2017. The contest is hosted by Kyiv, Ukraine, and produced by the Ukrainian broadcaster UA:PBC.\nL28:   * Place: Kyiv International Exhibition Centre, Kyiv, Ukraine\nL29:   * Participants: 42\nL30:   * 【53†Semi-final 1】: Took place on 9 May 2017 with 18 participants. The 10 songs with highest points advanced to the Grand Final\nL31:   * 【54†Semi-final 2】: Took place on 11 May 2017 with 18 participants. The 10 songs with highest points advanced to the Grand Final\nL32:   * 【26†Grand Final】: Takes place on 13 May 2017 with 26 participants; Ukraine (host), Big-5 (Germany, Spain, France, Italy and United Kingdom), 10 best from Semi-Final 1, 10 best from Semi-Final 2\nL33: 【17†Running order】【18†Kyiv 2017】【19†Draw】【20†Grand Final】【21†UA:PBC】【22†EBU】\nL34: \nL35: Found an error in the text? Please let us know\nL36: ## Eurovision News\nL37: \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEurovision 2018: Running order in the Grand Final decided (https://eurovisionworld.com/esc/eurovision-2018-running-order-in-grand-final-decided)\nciteturn35view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://eurovisionworld.com/esc/eurovision-2018-running-order-in-grand-final-decided\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 58\nL0:  | 【0†Eurovision News】【1†Junior Eurovision】【2†Eurovision Asia】【3†Burgas 2027】【4†Calendar】【5†National Selections】【6†Tickets】【7†Results & Points】【8†Odds】【9†Songs & Videos】【10†Polls】【11†Stats】【12†Winners】【13†Facts】【14†Quiz】【15†OGAE】select year/country  |\nL1: \nL2: \nL3: \nL4: 【16†RUNNING ORDER】\nL5: \nL6: # Eurovision 2018: Running order in the Grand Final decided\nL7: ## From Ukraine to Italy. The running order in the Grand Final of Eurovision Song Contest 2018 has been decided. Like the five previous years, the producer of Eurovision Song Contest decides the running order\nL8: \nL9: 11 May 2018\nL10: \nL11: Tags:【16†Running order】【17†Draw】【18†Grand Final】【19†UA:PBC】【20†EBU】【21†Lisbon 2018】\nL12: The producer of this years Eurovision, the Portuguese broadcaster RTP, has decided the running order for the Grand Final at Eurovision Song Contest 2018. The last five years the producers of the shows have decided the running order based on an allocation draw. The 【22†allocation draw took place】 shortly after 【23†Semi-final 1】 and 【24†Semi-final 2】. Here the participants were distributed in the first or second half of the Grand Final.\nL13: \nL14: 【25†EUROVISION 2018 • RUNNING ORDERGrand Final • 12 May 2018】\nL15: 【26†1Ukraine】【27†2Spain】【28†3Slovenia】【29†4Lithuania】【30†5Austria】【31†6Estonia】【32†7Norway】【33†8Portugal】【34†9United Kingdom】【35†10Serbia】【36†11Germany】【37†12Albania】【38†13France】\nL16: \nL17: 【39†14Czechia】【40†15Denmark】【41†16Australia】【42†17Finland】【43†18Bulgaria】【44†19Moldova】【45†20Sweden】【46†21Hungary】【47†22Israel】【48†23Netherlands】【49†24Ireland】【50†25Cyprus】【51†26Italy】\nL18: \nL19: This is the third year in a row that the song that closes Semi-final 2 opens the Grand Final. This year it's Ukraine.\nL20: ### How is the running order decided?\nL21: \nL22: Right after the 10 qualifiers from the second Semi-final are known, the producer of the contest starts laying the puzzle to ensure variety in the Grand Final\nL23: ### Eurovision Song Contest 2018\nL24: \nL25: The 63rd Eurovision Song Contest takes place on 8, 10 and 12 May 2018. The contest is hosted by Lisbon, Portugal, and produced by the Portuguese broadcaster RTP.\nL26:   * 【52†Place】: Altice Arena, Lisbon, Portugal\nL27:   * 【53†Participants】: 43\nL28:   * 【54†Semi-final 1】: 8 May 2018 – 19 participants: The 10 songs with highest points qualified to the Grand Final\nL29:   * 【55†Semi-final 2】: 10 May 2018 – 18 participants: The 10 songs with highest points qualified to the Grand Final\nL30:   * 【25†Grand Final】: 12 May 2018. 26 participants: Portugal (host), Big-5 (Germany, Spain, France, Italy and United Kingdom), 10 best from Semi-Final 1, 10 best from Semi-Final 2\nL31: 【16†Running order】【17†Draw】【18†Grand Final】【19†UA:PBC】【20†EBU】【21†Lisbon 2018】\nL32: \nL33: Found an error in the text? Please let us know\nL34: ## Eurovision News\nL35: \nL36: 【13†Did you know...Eurovision 2026 had 35 participating countries – the lowest number since the introduction of Semi-finals in 2004】\nL37: \nL38: 【13†Did you know...In 1981 the UK act Bucks Fizz stunned viewers with their Velcro rip-away skirts and within 48 hours, Velcro had sold out across the country】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEurovision 2022: Running order in the Grand Final (https://eurovisionworld.com/esc/eurovision-2022-running-order-in-the-grand-final)\nciteturn35view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://eurovisionworld.com/esc/eurovision-2022-running-order-in-the-grand-final\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 58\nL0:  | 【0†Eurovision News】【1†Junior Eurovision】【2†Eurovision Asia】【3†Burgas 2027】【4†Calendar】【5†Tickets】【6†National Selections】【7†Results & Points】【8†Odds】【9†Songs & Videos】 【10†Polls】【11†Stats】【12†Winners】【13†Facts】【14†Quiz】【15†OGAE】select year/country  |\nL1: \nL2: \nL3: \nL4: 【16†Image: Eurovision 2022 Grand Final Running Order†pix.eurovisionworld.com】\nL5: \nL6: 【17†RUNNING ORDER】\nL7: \nL8: # Eurovision 2022: Running order in the Grand Final\nL9: ## From the Czech Republic to Estonia: The running order in the Grand Final of the Eurovision Song Contest 2022 has been decided. Like the seven previous years, the producer of the Eurovision Song Contest has decided the running order\nL10: \nL11: 【18†Image: Eurovisionworld†pix.eurovisionworld.com】By Eurovisionworld 13 May 2022\nL12: \nL13: Tags:【17†Running order】【19†Draw】【20†Turin 2022】【21†EBU】\nL14: The producer of this year's Eurovision, Italian broadcaster RAI, has decided the running order for the Grand Final at the Eurovision Song Contest 2022. Over the last eight years, the shows' producers have decided the running order based on an allocation draw.\nL15: \nL16: A 【22†draw】 took place shortly after 【23†Semi-final 1】 and 【24†Semi-final 2】. Here, the participants were distributed in the first or second half of the Grand Final.\nL17: Right after the 10 qualifiers from the second Semi-final were decided, the producers of the contest started laying the puzzle to ensure variety in the Grand Final. And they took their time...\nL18: \nL19: 【25†EUROVISION 2022 • RUNNING ORDERGrand Final • 14 May 2022】\nL20: \nL21: 【26†1Czechia】【27†2Romania】【28†3Portugal】【29†4Finland】【30†5Switzerland】【31†6France】【32†7Norway】【33†8Armenia】【34†9Italy】【35†10Spain】【36†11Netherlands】【37†12Ukraine】【38†13Germany】\nL22: 【39†14Lithuania】【40†15Azerbaijan】【41†16Belgium】【42†17Greece】【43†18Iceland】【44†19Moldova】【45†20Sweden】【46†21Australia】【47†22United Kingdom】【48†23Poland】【49†24Serbia】【50†25Estonia】\nL23: ### Eurovision Song Contest 2022\nL24: \nL25: The 66th Eurovision Song Contest takes place on 10, 12 and 14 May 2022. The contest will be held in Turin, Italy, produced by Italian broadcaster RAI.\nL26:   * 【51†Location】: Pala Olimpico, Turin, Italy\nL27:   * 【51†Participants】: 40\nL28:   * 【52†Semi-final 1】: 10 May 2022 – 17 participants: The 10 best songs qualified to the Grand Final\nL29:   * 【53†Semi-final 2】: 12 May 2022 – 18 participants: The 10 best songs qualified to the Grand Final\nL30:   * 【25†Grand Final】: 14 May 2022 – 25 participants: Big-5 (Germany, Spain, France, Italy and the United Kingdom), 10 best from Semi-Final 1, 10 best from Semi-Final 2\nL31: \nL32: 【17†Running order】【19†Draw】【20†Turin 2022】【21†EBU】\nL33: Found an error in the text? Please let us know\nL34: ## Eurovision News\nL35: \nL36: 【13†Did you know...In 2015 Finland's song \"Aina Mun Pitää\" only runs for 1 minute and 27 seconds. The shortest song in the history of the Eurovision Song Contest】\nL37: \nL38: 【13†Did you know...Spain's cleverly titled, La La La from 1968 contained no fewer than 138 la's】\nL39: \nL40: 【13†Did you know...The largest number of nations to take part was 43 in 2008, 2011 and 2018】\nL41: \nL42: Select year or country\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEurovision 2023: Running order for the Grand Final (https://eurovisionworld.com/esc/eurovision-2023-running-order-in-the-grand-final)\nciteturn35view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://eurovisionworld.com/esc/eurovision-2023-running-order-in-the-grand-final\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 60\nL0:  | 【0†Eurovision News】【1†Junior Eurovision】【2†Burgas 2027】【3†Calendar】【4†National Selections】【5†Tickets】【6†Eurovision Asia】【7†Results & Points】【8†Odds】【9†Songs & Videos】【10†Polls】【11†Stats】【12†Winners】【13†Facts】【14†Quiz】【15†OGAE】select year/country  |\nL1: \nL2: \nL3: \nL4: 【16†Image: Eurovision 2023 Running Order†pix.eurovisionworld.com】\nL5: \nL6: 【17†RUNNING ORDER】\nL7: \nL8: # Eurovision 2023: Running order for the Grand Final\nL9: ## The running order for the Grand Final of the Eurovision Song Contest 2023 has been decided. Like the seven previous years, the producer of the Eurovision Song Contest has decided the running order\nL10: \nL11: 【18†Image: Eurovisionworld†pix.eurovisionworld.com】By Eurovisionworld 12 May 2023\nL12: \nL13: Tags:【17†Running order】【19†Draw】【20†Liverpool 2023】【21†EBU】【22†BBC】\nL14: The producer of this year's Eurovision, British broadcaster BBC, has decided the running order for the Grand Final at the Eurovision Song Contest 2023. The last nine years the producers of the shows have decided the running order based on an allocation draw.\nL15: \nL16: A 【23†draw】 took place shortly after 【24†Semi-final 1】 and 【25†Semi-final 2】. Here the participants were distributed in the first or second half of the Grand Final.\nL17: Right after the 10 qualifiers from the second Semi-final were decided, the producers of the contest started laying the puzzle to ensure variety in the Grand Final.\nL18: \nL19: It was already decided via a draw that Ukraine would perform as song number 19 and the United Kingdom would perform as number 26 in the Grand Final.\nL20: \nL21: 【26†EUROVISION 2023 • RUNNING ORDERGrand Final • 13 May 2023】\nL22: 【27†1Austria】【28†2Portugal】【29†3Switzerland】【30†4Poland】【31†5Serbia】【32†6France】【33†7Cyprus】【34†8Spain】【35†9Sweden】【36†10Albania】【37†11Italy】【38†12Estonia】【39†13Finland】\nL23: \nL24: 【40†14Czechia】【41†15Australia】【42†16Belgium】【43†17Armenia】【44†18Moldova】【45†19Ukraine】【46†20Norway】【47†21Germany】【48†22Lithuania】【49†23Israel】【50†24Slovenia】【51†25Croatia】【52†26United Kingdom】\nL25: ### Eurovision Song Contest 2023\nL26: \nL27: The 67th Eurovision Song Contest takes place on 9, 11 and 13 May 2023. The contest will be held in Liverpool, United Kingdom, and produced by British broadcaster BBC.\nL28:   * 【53†Location】: Liverpool, United Kingdom\nL29:   * 【53†Participants】: 37\nL30:   * 【54†Semi-final 1】: 9 May – 15 participants: The 10 best songs qualified for the Grand Final\nL31:   * 【55†Semi-final 2】: 11 May – 16 participants: The 10 best songs qualified for the Grand Final\nL32:   * 【26†Grand Final】: 13 May – 26 participants: Ukraine, Big-5 (Germany, Spain, France, Italy and the United Kingdom), 10 best from Semi-Final 1, 10 best from Semi-Final 2\nL33: \nL34: 【17†Running order】【19†Draw】【20†Liverpool 2023】【21†EBU】【22†BBC】\nL35: Found an error in the text? Please let us know\nL36: ## Eurovision News\nL37: \nL38: 【13†Did you know...The youngest ever winner was 13-year-old Sandra Kim from Belgium who won Eurovision in 1986】\nL39: \nL40: 【13†Did you know...In the first ever Eurovision Song Contest (1956), Luxembourg asked Switzerland to vote on its behalf. And the winner was: Switzerland!】\nL41: \nL42: 【13†Did you know...All Eurovision songs must not be longer than three minutes】\nL43: \nL44: Select year or country\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEurovision 2024: Running order for the Grand Final (https://eurovisionworld.com/esc/eurovision-2024-running-order-for-the-grand-final)\nciteturn35view6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://eurovisionworld.com/esc/eurovision-2024-running-order-for-the-grand-final\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 67\nL0:  | 【0†Eurovision News】【1†Junior Eurovision】【2†Eurovision Asia】【3†Burgas 2027】【4†Calendar】【5†National Selections】【3†Burgas 2027】【6†Tickets】【7†Results & Points】【8†Odds】【9†Songs & Videos】【10†Polls】【11†Stats】【12†Winners】【13†Facts】【14†Quiz】【15†OGAE】select year/country  |\nL1: \nL2: \nL3: \nL4: 【16†Image: Eurovision 2024 Running Order†pix.eurovisionworld.com】\nL5: \nL6: 【17†RUNNING ORDER】\nL7: \nL8: # Eurovision 2024: Running order for the Grand Final\nL9: ## The running order for the Grand Final of the Eurovision Song Contest 2024 has been decided. Like the 10 previous years, the producer of the Eurovision Song Contest has decided the running order\nL10: \nL11: 【18†Image: Eurovisionworld†pix.eurovisionworld.com】By Eurovisionworld 10 May 2024\nL12: Updated 11 May 2024 11 May 2024\nL13: \nL14: Tags:【17†Running order】【19†Draw】【20†Malmö 2024】【21†EBU】【22†SVT】\nL15: \nL16: UPDATE 11 MAY 2024, 14:15 CEST\nL17: ### Disqualification of the Netherlands\nL18: \nL19: After the disqualification of the Netherlands' Joost Klein, the number of competing countries in the Grand Final has now been reduced from 26 to 25.\nL20: \nL21: All contestants keep their number in the official running order. There will be NO song in position number 5.\nL22: The producer of this year's Eurovision, Swedish broadcaster SVT, has decided the running order for the Grand Final at the Eurovision Song Contest 2024. Over the last 10 years the shows' producers have decided the running order based on an allocation draw.\nL23: A 【23†draw】 took place shortly after 【24†Semi-final 1】 and 【25†Semi-final 2】. Here, half of the participants were distributed in the first or second half of the Grand Final. The other half was in the category \"Producer Decides,\" meaning that the Swedish producer SVT could freely decide where to put these countries in the running order.\nL24: \nL25: Right after the 10 qualifiers from the second Semi-final were decided, the producers of the contest started laying the puzzle to ensure variety in the Grand Final.\nL26: It had already been decided via a draw that Sweden would perform as song number 1 in the Grand Final.\nL27: \nL28: 【26†EUROVISION 2024 • RUNNING ORDERGrand Final • 11 May 2024】\nL29: \nL30: 【27†1Sweden】【28†2Ukraine】【29†3Germany】【30†4Luxembourg】【31†6Israel】【32†7Lithuania】【33†8Spain】【34†9Estonia】【35†10Ireland】【36†11Latvia】【37†12Greece】【38†13United Kingdom】【39†14Norway】\nL31: 【40†15Italy】【41†16Serbia】【42†17Finland】【43†18Portugal】【44†19Armenia】【45†20Cyprus】【46†21Switzerland】【47†22Slovenia】【48†23Croatia】【49†24Georgia】【50†25France】【51†26Austria】\nL32: ### Eurovision Song Contest 2024\nL33: \nL34: The 68th Eurovision Song Contest takes place on 7, 9 and 11 May 2024. The contest is being held in Malmö, Sweden, and produced by Swedish broadcaster SVT.\nL35:   * 【52†Location】: Malmö, Sweden\nL36:   * 【52†Participants】: 37\nL37:   * 【53†Semi-final 1】: 7 May – 15 participants: The 10 best songs qualified for the Grand Final\nL38:   * 【54†Semi-final 2】: 9 May – 16 participants: The 10 best songs qualified for the Grand Final\nL39:   * 【26†Grand Final】: 11 May – 25 participants: Sweden, Big-5 (Germany, Spain, France, Italy and the United Kingdom), 10 best from Semi-final 1, 10 best from Semi-final 2 (minus Netherlands due to 【55†disqualification】)\n"
